nst me.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ@Thou liftest me up to the wind; thou causest me to ride upon it,¦layout ‚¤text¼And dissolvest my substance.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ,For I know that thou wilt bring me to death,¦layout ‚¤textÙ*And to the house appointed for all living.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses˜„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines’‚¤textÙ6Howbeit he will not stretch out his hand to the grave,¦layout ‚¤textÙ#Though they cry in his destruction.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ+Did not I weep for him that was in trouble?¦layout ‚¤textÙ%Was not my soul grieved for the poor?¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ/When I looked for good, then evil came unto me:¦layout ‚¤textÙ1And when I waited for light, there came darkness.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ!My bowels boiled, and rested not:¦layout ‚¤textÙ$The days of affliction prevented me.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ I went mourning without the sun:¦layout ‚¤textÙ,I stood up, and I cried in the congregation.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textºI am a brother to dragons,¦layout ‚¤text¸And a companion to owls.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤text¹My skin is black upon me,¦layout ‚¤textÙ"And my bones are burned with heat.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ#My harp also is turned to mourning,¦layout ‚¤textÙ.And my organ into the voice of them that weep.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse